# 3D & WebGL Canvas

Keep heavy 3D in `components/canvas/`. Load every React Three Fiber `<Canvas>` with `next/dynamic` and `ssr: false`.

```tsx
const ShowcaseCanvas = dynamic(
  () => import("@/components/canvas/ShowcaseCanvas"),
  { ssr: false, loading: () => <ShowcaseLoader /> }
);
```

Gate heavy assets with a custom `<Html>` loader from `@react-three/drei`. Keep it quiet and precise: thin type, tracked labels, progress only.

```tsx
function AssetLoader() {
  const { progress } = useProgress();
  return (
    <Html center>
      <p className="text-xs tracking-[0.3em] text-white/70">
        {Math.round(progress)}%
      </p>
    </Html>
  );
}
```

Do not mount `<Canvas>` directly in a Server Component or outside `components/canvas/`.
